Subject: [PATCH 7/7] media: qcom: camss: a metadata node beside each RDI video node

Embedded metadata reaches an RDI like any other stream, but applications
expect it on a metadata capture node next to the image node, as the Tegra
VI patch provides on Jetson.

Every RDI line of a 17x VFE gets a second video device, msm_vfeN_metaM, of
type V4L2_BUF_TYPE_META_CAPTURE with the D4XX format. The line's source pad
links to its image node (enabled by default, no longer immutable) or to its
metadata node, never both, so the line feeds whichever node is linked.

A metadata buffer is as large as the lines of the subdev the node is linked
to. The node keeps its format in the multi-planar form the VFE reads and
translates it at the ioctls, so the capture path is unchanged.

The metadata nodes register after all image nodes, which keeps the image
nodes' device numbers.

Two nodes now share one line's buffer list, so the node that is not linked
must never reach it. vb2 hands the driver a node's buffers after
prepare_streaming and before start_streaming; the media pipeline therefore
starts in prepare_streaming, where the link is tested once with the graph
held, and stops in unprepare_streaming. An unlinked node is refused there,
before any of its buffers is queued.
